      "writtenOn": "2020-07-15T20:08:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, I should change the priority of that init since we don\u0027t know what DB we have (and therefore how many charger chips we have) until CBI FW_CONFIG is retrieved also during I2C+1 priority.\n\nWe\u0027re trying to keep the time spend in extpower_is_present() short since it\u0027s called a lot.  We can switch to an i2c call-out if the proposed patch is unacceptable though.\n\nEven when we correctly detect that external power is present on boot, we still seem to be booting anyway.  I included an annotated EC log from a run here: https://paste.googleplex.com/5273387284824064\n\nAnd same behavior comes up on waddledee: https://paste.googleplex.com/5658493447045120",
